  "title": "Israeli Election 2026: Netanyahu's Rivals and Key Parties",
  "summary": "Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's Likud party and its allies won 53 seats, falling short of the majority needed to form a government, while Gadi Eisenkot's opposition bloc secured 48 seats, leaving a path unclear. The election, seen as a test of Netanyahu's leadership, has led to a deadlock between his coalition and the opposition.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's Likud party and its allies won 53 seats in the parliamentary elections, falling short of the majority needed to form a government.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Gadi Eisenkot's opposition bloc secured 48 seats, leaving a path to form a government unclear.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The election was held on Tuesday, with Prime Minister Netanyahu seeking to retain power amid concerns over foreign interference and domestic policy.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
