      "title": "Herzog to meet Israeli election rivals as decision nears on path to power",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/05/herzog-netanyahu-eisenkot-israel-election-decision",
      "description": "<p>President calls on all parties to help avoid new election after Netanyahu and Eisenkot blocs fell short of majority</p><p>Israel’s president, Isaac Herzog, was due to meet Benjamin Netanyahu and his chief political rival, Gadi Eisenkot, on Thursday with less than a week left before he decides which of the two men should first try to form a government.</p><p>A bitterly contested election last month, seen by many observers as one of the most consequential for Israel in many decades, ended with neither Netanyahu nor Eisenkot, a former military general and chief of staff, securing a clear pathway to power.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/05/herzog-netanyahu-eisenkot-israel-election-decision\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-05T18:13:01"
    },
